rd no production bugs (or almost none if any but anyways etc) (at least much more than in base advciv +/- civ4 if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc)), they produce too much units, so barbarians are a nice help for that goal so that AIs don't go bankrupt too soon and that they can grow more earlier due to having less units as counter intuitive as it may seem, especially since barbarians should burn a bunch of the early and not so useful later units like ancient macemen, archers, longbowmen, etc, so should hopefully help a lot, and AIs are now seemingly (more than in this case i mean but anyways etc) strong enough to defend well or well enough even against such strong barbarians so hopefully helpful but anyways etc.
